Zero-padding-bit JBRD wiring — task #11 (2026-05-28)
====================================================

Goal
----

Close the last residual DIFF on the 200-file JPEG-in-JXL recompression
bench (`jpeg_in_jxl_recompression_2026-05-28.tsv`): `20230706_124619.jpg`,
a baseline (SOF0) JPEG with DRI restart markers. Source has `0x00`
bytes as entropy-stream padding before its RST markers; our
reconstruction previously emitted `0x7F` / `0x3F` (the spec-default
"all-1-bit" padding), producing a 3-byte diff per file (one per RST
boundary that had a non-byte-aligned entropy-segment end).

This is the `JpegData.has_zero_padding_bit` + `JpegData.padding_bits`
JBRD signal in libjxl, distinct from task #10's `reset_points` +
`extra_zero_runs` work. libjxl tracks per-segment padding bits via
`BitReaderState::FinishStream` (`enc_jpeg_data_reader.cc:441-470`)
and replays them through `JumpToByteBoundary`
(`dec_jpeg_data_writer.cc:139-159`) on the decode side. zenjpeg did
not yet expose those bits; this chunk plumbs them through both
crates.

Scope
-----

Two repos changed:

  zenjpeg (sibling worktree `zenjpeg--zero-padding-bit-zj/`, 0.8.6+):

    - New `BitReader::partial_byte_padding_bits()` helper extracts
      the current partial-byte unconsumed bits (MSB-first), without
      mutating state. Mirrors libjxl `FinishStream`'s `npadbits`
      extraction.
    - New `EntropyDecoder::partial_byte_padding_bits()` forwards.
    - `JbrdMetadata` extended with `has_zero_padding_bit: bool` and
      `padding_bits: Vec<u8>` fields (libjxl-named, libjxl-semantic).
    - `JpegParser` gains `jbrd_padding_bits: Option<Vec<u8>>` and
      pad-bit append helpers; `enable_jbrd_tracking()` now also
      enables pad-bit accumulation.
    - Capture sites threaded:
        * `decode_scan` (baseline / extended sequential): per-RST
          and end-of-scan.
        * `decode_dc_scan_non_interleaved` /
          `decode_dc_scan_interleaved` (progressive DC scans):
          per-RST.
        * `decode_ac_first_scan_tracked` /
          `decode_ac_refine_scan_tracked` (progressive AC scans):
          per-RST.
        * `decode_progressive_scan`: end-of-scan, mirrors the
          baseline path.
    - `decode_coefficients_with_jbrd_metadata()` takes the
      accumulated bits, sets `has_zero_padding_bit` iff ANY bit is
      0 (libjxl's `JPEGData::VisitFields` semantic at
      `jpeg_data.cc:368-380`), and clears `padding_bits` when the
      flag is false to keep the JBRD payload compact.
    - 6 new bit-stream unit tests cover the helper (empty / all-0
      / all-1 / mixed / read-only / counts).

  jxl-encoder (sibling worktree `jxl-encoder--zero-padding-bit/`):

    - `Cargo.toml` `[patch.crates-io].zenjpeg` re-points at the
      zenjpeg sibling. Path-pin will revert once zenjpeg 0.8.6
      lands on main.
    - `jpeg/parse.rs::extract_coefficients_zenjpeg` reads the new
      `JbrdMetadata.has_zero_padding_bit` / `padding_bits` and
      copies them to `JpegData`. The JBRD writer at
      `jpeg/jbrd.rs:203-211` already serialises both fields
      correctly — only the parse-side population was missing.

Build
-----

  cd /home/lilith/work/zen/jxl-encoder--zero-padding-bit
  cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder-cli \
    --no-default-features \
    --features 'jpeg-reencoding,parallel,jxl_encoder/std'

  Same `--no-default-features` requirement as the original bench
  (the local butteraugli sibling has uncommitted in-progress
  modules that block the default build). Out of scope here.

Run
---

  cjxl-rs <src.jpg> <out.jxl> -e 5 -d 0
  djxl <out.jxl> <recon.jpg>
  cmp <src.jpg> <recon.jpg>     # must match byte-for-byte

Bench script: see `/tmp/t11/bench_roundtrip.py` (200-file driver).

